{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "26", "m": "07", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "04", "S": "16"}}, "news": [{"title": "DC orders closure of illegal homestays in Mysuru", "para": "Mysuru deputy commissioner ordered stringent safety measures for all homestays. Unregistered establishments must shut down immediately and obtain necessary approvals. Surprise inspections will verify safety protocols and guest record maintenance. Emergency contact numbers will be prominently displayed for tourist assistance. Tourists are advised to stay only in registered and licensed accommodations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/hospitality/mysuru-clamps-down-on-illegal-homestays-after-tourist-assault/132624099?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1305575/132624099.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "hospitality"}, {"title": "Prayagraj civic body to rollout OTS scheme for property tax defaulters from Aug 15", "para": "Prayagraj Municipal Corporation will launch a one-time settlement scheme for outstanding taxes. Property owners can clear pending dues in three installments after applying. The scheme benefits approximately 90,000 property owners, including long-term defaulters. This initiative aims to improve tax recovery and boost civic body revenue. The scheme will be available from August 15 to December 15.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/prayagraj-municipal-corporation-launches-ots-scheme-for-property-tax-defaulters/132624052?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-638474/132624052.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Manesar civic body to map PGs & guesthouses built in residential zones", "para": "Gurugram municipality will recover property tax from unauthorized paying guests and guesthouses.  Officials will conduct surveys and seal properties if tax dues remain unpaid.  The corporation aims to recover Rs 229 crore from its top 100 defaulters.  Improving property tax collections is critical for civic infrastructure development projects.  The horticulture branch will also restore ponds and increase rainwater harvesting pits.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/manesar-civic-body-cracks-down-on-unauthorized-pgs-and-guesthouses/132624018?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1412771/132624018.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}